    "body": "## Summary\n- Fixes CSV exports that put YouTube timestamp labels (e.g. \"17 seconds\", \"1 minute, 1 second\") in the Text column instead of actual captions\n- Parses human-readable transcript timestamps correctly and stops generating fake 1-second start times\n- Falls back to InnerTube API when transcript panel scraping returns timestamps without caption text\n\n## Install\nDownload `subtidex.zip` below → unzip → **Load unpacked** on `chrome://extensions/`\n\n## Test plan\n- [ ] Reload extension and hard-refresh a YouTube watch page\n- [ ] Extract captions from a video with the transcript panel open\n- [ ] Confirm CSV Text column contains spoken caption sentences, not duration labels"
